A||||8||87GT||Something goofy goin on||||9||
Z||000000||87GT||12-06-1999||02:16 PM||||Okay here is the problem, I am going down the road today in my 87GT when I notice that my tach is dancing around doing weird stuff and then I begin to notice a really bad miss in the engine.  It does not do this at idle.  I have called my cousin who does the mechanicing on the car and he said something about a module going out?  I would like to see what some of you think it is.  I am sure somebody has had this happen before.  I am depressed. 8-(||||reg||9
Z||000001||deceler8||12-06-1999||02:23 PM||||TACH FILTER TACH FILTER TACH FILTER<P>Unplug the tach filter (little can that looks like an old fashioned ignition condenser...believe it's down in the coil area...someone else can give a better idea on the V6...I've got a four)...<P>Tach won't work with this unplugged, but if your miss goes away, you've nailed the problem.<P>Search the forum under "tach filter" for more info on this component.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GT||12-06-1999||03:09 PM||||Okay, I think I have located it.  On the V6 models, is it the little cylinder looking thing on the lower right side of the coil?  If it is, I cant get the damn think to unplug, can somebody please verify that this is it. Thanks for you info deceler8||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GT||12-06-1999||03:09 PM||||Okay, I think I have located it.  On the V6 models, is it the little cylinder looking thing on the lower right side of the coil?  If it is, I cant get the damn thing to unplug, can somebody please verify that this is it. Thanks for you info deceler8||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GT||12-06-1999||04:16 PM||||Hey Deceler8, I went ahead and finally got the plug off.  I went out for a spin and the problem is gone.  Thanks a lot!  I dont know what some of us would do if not for this forum. I was considering driving a mini van to work tomorrow.. uughh||||reg||12
Z||000005||dogtired||12-06-1999||04:30 PM||||Thats it, Thats the thing?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Had to look it up in the 22P. I thought it was a condenser, but the book says "FILTER, Tach Signal" P/N 10040110. On my V6 I have one off a 4cyl (just cause I had one) & it works OK.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||12-06-1999||05:54 PM||||Yep, that $0.30 worth of electronic components thingy called "Tach Filter" can cause quite a lot of problems...||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||12-06-1999||08:29 PM||||Friends,<P>Could the tach filter cause severe missing on a DIS equipped L-4?  I will further describe my symptoms.  When the engine is cold (based on ambient temperature.. i.e. does not happen in summer when air is warm and dry) upon acceleration, the engine has severe stumbling problems.  The problem lies in since my vehicle is equipt with an automatic (groan) when selecting gears the engine will stall from this initial stumble coupled with the standard drop of rpms when put under load of the torque converter.  After the vehicle has reached its operating temperature/closed loop mode, it drives fine.  No trouble codes are set.  I have been living with this problem for well over a year now, and just have to warm the car for a few minutes before driving.  I am sure that it is an electrical problem but have not been able to properly diagnose it.  <P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||12-07-1999||09:29 AM||||I dont think the 4 bangers were equipped with   external tach filters, but maybe someone can verify that (batboy, ogre?).  You may be suffering from a bad or almost bad coil pack.||||reg||1
